    "updated_at": "2022-06-14T07:37:50Z",
    "body": "So ip-regex would return \"not IPv4\" for https://jsdom.github.io/whatwg-url/#url=aHR0cHM6Ly8x77yOMS4xLjEv&base=YWJvdXQ6Ymxhbms= (note the ． (U+FF0E)), but the host parser would return an IPv4 address. A standalone `parseIPvv4` might also return \"not IPv4\" if it directly invokes the IPv4 parser. That seems problematic.\r\n\r\nCan you elaborate on why `URLHost` would not satisfy these use cases?",
